    {
      "date": "2026-09-05",
      "what": "Analysis seat moved from claude-code.opus-5 to codex.gpt-5.6-luna, the first-block analysis model. Seed 736 replaced by 748.",
      "why": "In the first dialogue (seed 736, world 101, bare) Opus 5 in the analysis seat returned a semantic event with target_id unspecified together with a non-empty public_identifier_ids list on turn 4 in 3 of 3 tries and on turn 6 in 2 of 3 tries. The strict validator (services/adaptiveWarrantSemanticEvents.js, rule target:unspecified_cannot_name_public_identifiers) rejects that pair, so turn 4 stayed unread, the coverage guard quarantined the dialogue, and the run stopped. The dialogue also used exactly its 30-call cap. Luna hit this form once in the pilot and never in the 576-turn first block. The registration forbids coercing a response into shape and allows one retake per dialogue, which the second attempt used.",
      "what_it_changes": "Tutor and learner seats are still the second family (Opus 5). The analysis seat, which feeds the gate and the learner record, is the same model as the first block. A result now speaks to the tutor and learner seats only; it cannot separate the analysis seat from the first block.",
      "ruling": "User ruling in chat, 2026-09-05: luna in the analysis seat, amend and GO.",
